Z||000000||sjp777||05-23-2001||09:04 PM||||Just saw a report about Sarah Fisher on the news.<P>20 years old, part time college student, and she's running in her 2nd Indy 500 this year. According to the report, she has previously finished 2nd and 3rd in Indy car races and actually has a decent shot to place in the top ten or even take the checker.<P>Now wouldn't that be cool?<P>Hey Lisa, ever think about gettin a job like that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Black88GT||05-23-2001||09:12 PM||||Not sure what this has to do with Fiero's (General Fiero Chat) but...<P>I was watching this show on HBO about her.  Seems like the all too common case of "Father wants son, gets daughter, figures he will turn daughter into son".  I've seen that way too much since I played sports.  She started racing at the age of like 8 or something.  I am hard pressed to believe some 8 year old just says "hey instead of soccer I want to race cars", boy or girl.  And in the HBO show they said she got her sponsorship from a guy that is known for sponsoring drivers that aren't the typical race/gender. Not trying to take away anything from her its just the way I see it.  ||||reg||1
