Z||000027||mblackwell||05-24-2001||05:30 PM||||I know Sarah Fisher.  Well nt really, I went to high school with her and I see her mom all the time.  Some kid in my brother's 5th grade class had one of her gocarts, but he sold it.  His teacher was POed about that.<P>I live about 5 minutes away from Commercial Point.  Her mom is a computer teacher at Teays Valley Middle School, and teahces PC repair at the high school.  I currently have a horrible job installing PCs for the school district.||||reg||1
Z||000028||kslish||05-24-2001||10:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>She started racing at the age of like 8 or something.  I am hard pressed to believe some 8 year old just says "hey instead of soccer I want to race cars", boy or girl.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay, I can't believe I'm going to post this as it may get me flamed for my opinions, but I spent most of today on the road and I'm a little irritable.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>In defense of Sarah, do you think Tiger Woods just picked up a set of golf clubs on his own when he started at age 4 or whatever?  No, it was his father that taught him the basics and encouraged him.  I think it was the same with Sarah, I'm sure if she didn't like it she would have quit a long time ago.  Same with Tiger.  But their parents at least gave them the opportunity to do it and find out that they were good at it.<P>I'm all for Sarah as far as the attention she gets as a race car driver.  Hopefully it'll encourage other talented females to get involved in the sport.  I enjoyed the fact that there were two women in last years 500, although they managed to take each other out...<P>However, I don't think Fisher is a perfect driver.  Far from it.  She qualifies extremely well when she is the only one on the track, but she sometimes gets careless during the race, getting herself or others into trouble.  Maybe it's just a lack of experience and she'll outgrow it.  She also tested a CART Champ car for Derek Walker and she had serious trouble with the extra power a CART car has, so she has a ways to go before she is among the elite.<P>I'm still trying to figure out who to pull for in this year's 500 since my man Montoya went to F1.  It'll probably be one of the boys from CART.<P>After all, real race car drivers can turn left AND right.  Hehehe....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>P.S. - Any opinions stated in this post are purely my own and aren't meant to bash anyone else's opinion...it's just how I feel.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Eric||05-25-2001||12:58 AM||||Could Michael win the 500 this year?  I'd personally love to see him do it, but I don't think it would mean as much now as it would have in the early '90s when the race really still meant something.  Hell, Montoya seemingly came out of oblivion to win the race last year.  Obviously he's one of the most talented drivers ever to hit the brickyard, but to dominate American motor racing like he did is something all racing fans should respect and admire.<P>I want to go on the record as saying that I believe Sarah Fisher is a talented driver and has potential.  I'd like to see her make an attempt at CART.  I don't know if she'd adapt if only because she's not a road racer by training.  <P>I'm still of the opinion; however, that a great racing driver is just someone who's completely fearless.  I grew up across the street from an Indy car driver.  Nevermind his intelligence or incredibly fast reflexs, his balls-to-the-wall driving style was what made him a commodity at the Brickyard.  I got to witness a few laps of his on opening qualifying weekend in '88 or '89.  While driving (fighting) an ill handling car, he was able to turn some relativly quick lap times.  Unfortunaly, he didn't put four together, and balled up the car in turn one the following weekend thus ending his racing career.  <P>My theory remains: to be an exceptional racing driver, you must be exceptional at everything AND fearless.  If Sarah Fisher is all of these things, we will certainly se great things from her.  It is still my opinion that she will never make it to F1.  Sorry rayb.<P>Raydar, I meant she can't compete in the world of Formula one, not Indy.  Everyone needs to step back and take an objective look at American motor racing versus the rest of the world.  Since Nascar and oval racing is the big thing now in this country, we automatically assume that these American icons could, if given the opportunity, compete on the world stage in the greatest racing series ever concieved.  I'm saying they're not one in the same.  CART comes very close to bridging the gap, but falls short only because of funding and driver talent issues.  I love open wheel racing, and if I sound bitter about indy cars and the 500, it is because I hate the fact that everything was split in two.<P>Sorry if I sound too sexist, Roger.  It's just that I feel this is the one place where I can vent my opinions without being judged by the politically correct crowd.  The only female I can think of who would read my posts is Lisa, and I don't really care to sweet talk to her (no offense, Lisa or anyone else who likes to sweet talk to her  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  It's just that I've been here for two years now, and I'm hard set in my ways.  And now that I think about it, I don't nearly as much as I should.  Girls tend to dislike this side of my personallity.  Sometimes I wish I could just beat this part of me into submission, but that would be a futile response and I probably wouldn't be able to walk for a week or two either.  <P>Isn't it obvious I don't get out much.  Look how long this post is.  I'm gonna go cry now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000030||Black88GT||05-25-2001||02:13 AM||||Tiger Woods is different and I will tell you why.  Look at what Tiger has become.  He is the best player now and in a couple years will probably be revered as the best EVER.  I don't watch racing but from what I saw on the show, she is lucky to QUALIFY.  So being the best ever and being mediocre are far from the same.  I am sure she is talented but I think if she was destined to be the best ever we would have heard something by now.  Also Tiger didn't get sponsored because he was a minority he was sponsored on merit.  There's something to be said about that.<P>||||reg||1
